# Silvergill Peddler {2}{U} (three Moxen, turn 1): "Whenever this creature becomes tapped, draw a card, then discard a card" (CR 603.2,
# 701.9). Casting it does nothing; attacking on turn 3 taps it, so Bot1 draws the Forest and discards a card: the hand stays the same size
# (after the turn-3 draw it holds 4 cards, and still 4 after the loot), and one card went to the graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Silvergill Peddler
Island x3
Forest
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Silvergill Peddler.Cast
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
? Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 4
Bot1.Attack(Silvergill Peddler > Bot2)
Bot1.Choose(Island)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 4
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Silvergill Peddler.Tapped = true
